title: SPIR-V Specification
author: John Kessenich, Google
author: Boaz Ouriel, Intel
author: Raun Krisch, Intel
changes:

=== Changes from Version 1.2, Revision 3

Fixed Khronos-internal issues:

- #249: Improve description of <<OpTranspose, *OpTranspose*>>.
- #251: Undefined values in <<OpUndef, *OpUndef*>> include abstract and opaque values.
- #258: Deprecate <<OpAtomicCompareExchangeWeak, *OpAtomicCompareExchangeWeak*>> in favor of <<OpAtomicCompareExchange, *OpAtomicCompareExchange*>>.
- #241: Use "invalid" instead of "compile-time" error for *ConstOffsets*.
- #248: <<OpImageSparseRead, *OpImageSparseRead*>> is not for *SubpassData*.
- #257: Allow *OpImageSparseFetch* and *OpImageSparseRead* with the *Sample* <<Image_Operands, image operands>>.
- #229: Some sensible constraints on branch hints for <<OpBranchConditional, *OpBranchConditional*>>.
- #236: <<OpVariable, *OpVariable*>>'s storage class must match storage class of the pointer type.
- #216: Can <<TypesVariables, decorate pointer types>> with *Coherent* and *Volatile*.
- #247: Don't say <<Scope_-id-, Scope _<id>_ >> is a mask; it is not.
- #254: Remove <<Validation, validation>> rules about the types atomic instructions can operate on. These rules belong instead to the client API.
- #265: <<OpGroupDecorate, *OpGroupDecorate*>> cannot target an *OpDecorationGroup*.
